"""LDhybrid v1.0 -- hybrid5 limb-darkening coefficients, MPS-ATLAS Set 2 (plane-parallel; Kostogryz et al. 2022), JWST_NIRSpec_G395H_NRS1 passband.

Standalone: needs only numpy; the coefficient grid is embedded.

    from ldhybrid_hybrid5_mps2_nirspec_g395h_nrs1 import coefficients, intensity
    r = coefficients(teff=5600, logg=4.4, mh=0.0)
    r = coefficients(5600, 4.4, 0.0, correction="B100G")
    r["coeffs"]      # (w1, w2, w3, w4, w5); also r["w"]
    r["q"]           # (q1, q2, q3, q4, q5): sampling coordinates in [0, 1]
    r["physical"]    # positive and monotonic?
    intensity(r["coeffs"], mu)                  # I(mu)/I(1)
    from_q(q), to_q(c)                          # unit hypercube <-> coefficients

Law (hybrid5):
    I(mu)/I(1) = 1 - w1 (1 - mu^4) - w2 (1 - mu^2)^2 - w3 P(mu; e0) - w4 P(mu; e1) - w5 P(mu; e2)
    P(mu; e) = [(mu^2 + e)^-2 - (1 + e)^-2] / [e^-2 - (1 + e)^-2]
    e0, e1, e2 = 0.0015965451792942786, 0.04127504477274302, 0.38743471584956696
Every shape falls from 1 at the limb to 0 at the centre, so the simplex
w >= 0, sum(w) <= 1 holds profiles with I(0) >= 0 that are non-increasing
towards the limb (a sufficient region: it is smaller than the set of all
positive monotonic hybrid5 profiles). Sampling coordinates: stick-breaking of
a flat Dirichlet, w_j = (1 - q_j^(1/(6-j))) prod_(i<j) q_i^(1/(6-i)),
j = 1..5; uniform q is a uniform prior over the simplex.

Coefficients: least squares uniform in projected radius (the transit-optimised
fit), constrained to that simplex. Grid: 16974 models, Teff 3500-7500 K,
log g 3.5-5.0, [M/H] -2.0 to +1.0.
Interpolation is linear on the Kuhn simplices of the (Teff, log g, [M/H])
tensor grid, as in ldhybrid.interpolate: continuous, exact at the models, and
a convex mix of four models (the law's physical region is convex, so a mix of
physical models is physical).
Outside the grid, coefficients() raises unless extrapolate=True (the nearest
model in Teff/100 K, log g/0.5, [M/H]/0.5).
lc_ppm is the light-curve error of the tabulated fits (p = 0.1).

correction: None (default) or a MURaM surface-field state, "ssd" (small-scale
dynamo), "B100G", "B200G", "B300G". For FGK stars LDhybrid recommends
MPS-ATLAS Set 2 + "B100G" (matches Kepler/TESS hosts); quiet Sun-like stars
prefer "ssd". MURaM covers 3196-6807 K at [M/H] = 0.
Generated by LDhybrid scripts/make_standalone.py from the v1.0 CDS tables.
The poles are the v1.0 values; check that any other hybrid5 implementation
uses the same three before passing these weights to it.
"""

